  "definition": "Sepsis is a life-threatening condition in which harmful microorganisms in the bloodstream trigger a rapidly worsening reaction throughout the body that can lead to shock. Common signs include fever, chills, fast heart rate, and rapid breathing, and it is a medical emergency needing urgent care.",
